<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'AI Model Inference with SageMaker & Serverless'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>AI Model Inference with SageMaker & Serverless</h1>
  <p>Deployed an ML model via SageMaker JumpStart and built a serverless API with Lambda and API Gateway for real-time predictions.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>SageMaker</span><span>Lambda</span><span>API Gateway</span><span>AI/ML</span><span>Serverless</span><span>Boto3</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/sagemaker-ai.png" alt="SageMaker AI Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates deploying a <strong>machine learning model</strong> via <strong>SageMaker JumpStart</strong> and exposing it through a <strong>serverless API</strong> for real-time inference without managing ML infrastructure.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Deployed Foundation Model (Meta Llama 2) using <strong>SageMaker JumpStart</strong>.</li>
      <li>Created a <strong>Lambda function</strong> to invoke the SageMaker endpoint.</li>
      <li>Set up <strong>API Gateway REST API</strong> to expose Lambda externally.</li>
      <li>Tested end-to-end with <strong>cURL/Postman</strong> for inference requests.</li>
      <li>Implemented <strong>IAM roles</strong> for secure endpoint invocation.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🌐 API Layer</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>API Gateway</strong> — REST API entry point</li>
          <li><strong>Lambda</strong> — Parses request, invokes endpoint</li>
          <li><strong>CORS headers</strong> — Cross-origin access</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🤖 ML Layer</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>SageMaker JumpStart</strong> — Pre-built Foundation Models</li>
          <li><strong>SageMaker Endpoint</strong> — Hosts and runs inference</li>
          <li><strong>Boto3 SDK</strong> — Programmatic invocation</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔐 Security</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>IAM Role</strong> — Lambda → SageMaker permission</li>
          <li><strong>Env variable</strong> — ENDPOINT_NAME</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Implementation Steps</h3>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">1</div><p>Created a SageMaker Domain and deployed <strong>Meta Llama 2 7B</strong> from JumpStart.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">2</div><p>Created Lambda with Python runtime and added <strong><code>sagemaker:InvokeEndpoint</code></strong> IAM policy.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">3</div><p>Set <strong>ENDPOINT_NAME</strong> environment variable in Lambda config.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">4</div><p>Created <strong>API Gateway REST API</strong> and linked to Lambda function.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">5</div><p>Tested with <strong>cURL</strong> sending JSON payload — confirmed real-time inference response.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Deployed Foundation Models using <strong>SageMaker JumpStart</strong> without training from scratch.</li>
      <li>Used <strong>Boto3 sagemaker-runtime</strong> to invoke endpoints programmatically.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>API Gateway + Lambda</strong> for serverless ML inference.</li>
      <li>Understood how to structure <strong>request/response payloads</strong> for LLM models.</li>
      <li>Always <strong>delete SageMaker endpoints</strong> when not in use to avoid charges.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

